Model weights are not distributed in this source repository. Each published
weight artifact must include a model card naming its base-model revision,
license, quantization process, recovery datasets, and redistribution terms.

Dataset records are not distributed in this source repository. Generated
dataset manifests retain per-record source and license metadata.

Qualcomm QNN and Hexagon SDK files are proprietary developer-supplied inputs
and must not be copied into this repository or its release archives.

The vendor directories intentionally contain no upstream sources until a
specific kernel family is pinned and its license is recorded next to the pin.

Vendored third-party source:

- models/qwen38_27b/vendor/cuda/ contains MIT-licensed CUDA MMQ/dequant
  reference files from llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp),
  pinned to revision ef2d770117db45b05aa7ecd1b0acca36370c5470,
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. The MIT license text and
  per-file digests are recorded next to the pin in
  models/qwen38_27b/vendor/cuda/LICENSE and
  models/qwen38_27b/vendor/cuda/UPSTREAM.json.

- models/qwen38_27b/vendor/cuda/syv_ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090/ contains an
  Apache-2.0 speculative-decode split-KV reference patch from syv-ai
  (https://github.com/syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090), pinned to revision
  60daef8255b6757d9791955a44bce27df1658ea6. Its immutable source digest and
  adaptation scope are recorded in the adjacent UPSTREAM.json. The patch is
  reference material only; CTOX does not link vLLM or Triton.

Direct driver binding dependency:

- The optional macOS `metal` feature uses metal-rs 0.33.0
  (https://github.com/gfx-rs/metal-rs), licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, as a thin
  binding to Apple's Metal API. It is not an inference framework. Exact direct
  and transitive versions are pinned in `models/qwen38_27b/Cargo.lock`.

Tokenizer dependency:

- The Qwen model crate uses Hugging Face tokenizers 0.23.1
  (https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers), licensed Apache-2.0, to execute
  the byte-verified model-specific BPE artifact. Default features are disabled;
  the build enables the pure-Rust `fancy-regex` path and does not enable HTTP,
  Oniguruma, progress reporting, or the C++ `esaxx_fast` feature. Exact direct
  and transitive versions are pinned in `models/qwen38_27b/Cargo.lock`.
